    },
    "body": "The project front doors and open issues mixed completed experiments with stale next steps, while the native model name, capability limits and remaining API/Studio work were difficult to find. This change presents **UOR-R4 Geometric Language Model**, makes the retained artifact and failed successor explicit, and codifies contextual lexical/role binding followed by shared state transitions and compositional emission.\n\nThe canonical plan and #820 now link twelve ordered responsibilities. All eleven previously open issues were rewritten with rationale, implementation, acceptance, dependencies and resource instructions; none was falsely closed. New #1172 and #1173 own native API/WASM and Pages Studio. The full 422-issue pre-change census and original open bodies are preserved. The 127-path README inventory records eighteen updated current entry points and 109 byte-identical historical/import/vendor files. The project map locates native source, mechanisms, research, artifacts and knowledge tooling. Historical front-door content remains linked at the original commit.\n\nAGENTS, contribution/workflow instructions, machine/readable policy and issue forms now use the same direction and preserve the existing standing authorization for necessary local allowance extensions. The complete continuation handoff binds model lineage, historical positives/negatives, source-reading requirements, cumulative resources, preservation and next steps. This is documentation and issue organization only: no model, Rust implementation, artifact or capability promotion changed.\n\nValidation: claim-wording check; existing native architecture-policy binary (no model behavior); YAML parsing of both issue forms; JSON parsing; git diff --check; 277 added local file links resolve; all thirteen current issue titles/bodies verified; all 422 prior issue states preserved; all 109 preserved README blobs match; retained/candidate SHA-256 and original checkout state match. Shared model ledger remains 4,387.536/4,410 seconds. No Cargo build, training, inference or broad QA was run. Protected CI status names are compatibility acknowledgements only.\n\nThe optional GitHub About description update was unavailable: the credential has push/triage access but no admin/maintain permission. README and repository documentation carry the new presentation.\n\nReferences #820, #973, #1139, #1140, #1172, #1173. All capability issues remain open until their full acceptance is met.\n",
